I always try not to anger shopkeepers, hence my knowledge 
on them is a bit limited.  However, some ideas:  

If you happen to have a lot of money (5000 gp?), it is 
possible that the shopkeeper will be pacified by using the 
(p)ay command.  However, this sounds a bit risky, hence I 
would make some trials in wizmode before trying (you have 
only precious few turns until the char is done for).  

IMHO, the next most elegant solution would be to use one 
or two scrolls of earth to trap the shopkeeper in.  If 
you hadn't been at the first Soko level, however, you almost 
certainly don't have the scrolls for this.  

The shopkeeper might or might not be subject to charm monster, 
though he will certainly become only peaceful.  Check in 
wizmode for his resistance against charming; if it's working 
more often than one in three trials, I'd give it a shot.  

In case this doesn't work, I would flee.  Neither pets nor 
protection is useful to a dead character (your ghost doesn't 
take over your protection or other intrinsics, AFAIK, hmmh, 
YANI..).  Use any available means to flee, since this means to 
survive.  Digging, teleport are best, running away is no good, 
the shopkeeper is way too fast.  

[If you happen to have a wand o tele, you might even be able 
to pull a simple trick:  First, port yourself out of the immediate 
reach, run for the downstairs, wait for or lure the shopkeeper 
there, go down, teleport the shopkeeper away (if this works, 
don't know about his/her MR, try in wizmode), go up; alternately, 
teleport yourself, wait until he/she comes close, then teleport 
yourself until you're close to the upstairs, go up.  You should 
end up with a 'deserted shop'.]

